# Handoffs are agent-first

When Josh asks for a handoff, do **not** write a human narrative or a bloggy procedure. Write a document another coding agent can execute with no back-and-forth.

Follow `.cursor/handoffs/TEMPLATE.md` exactly. Save the instance under `.cursor/handoffs/<slug>.md` and, if it is an operational loop, also as a skill in `.cursor/skills/<slug>/SKILL.md`.

Required sections, in this order: Receiver, Done when, Context (≤8 lines), Never, Inputs, Procedure (numbered, copy-pasteable), Verification, Report back, Stop and escalate.

Do not tell the receiving agent to "ask the user" for anything that is already in `kits.py`, `/config`, or this repo. Do not print secrets. Do not include slides.
